    "body": "## Problem\n\n`vim.opt_local.fileencoding:get()` fails with E21 after `:setlocal nomodifiable`. The getter uses a dry-run assignment to convert its saved value, so write validation can reject a read. Saved list values can also become unreadable after editor state changes, such as changing `ambiwidth`.\n\n## Solution\n\nExpose the existing `optval_to_obj()` converter as the internal, Lua-only `nvim__option_to_object()` function. Use it for `vim.opt` getters to convert the supplied saved value without assignment validation. The setter uses the same converter for its result. Copy values that are already structured so changing a returned table cannot change the saved option value.\n\nFixes #42393\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-19T12:42:44Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
