            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I first tried adding a conversion flag to `nvim_set_option_value()`, but that put too much into a single interface. Exposing the existing converter to Lua seemed clearer.\r\n\r\nEach `vim.opt` object already holds a saved value. That value can differ from the current option after another assignment or an infix operation. For example:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.opt.wildignore = { '*.swp' }\r\nlocal value = (vim.opt.wildignore + { '*.o' }):get()\r\n-- value is { '*.swp', '*.o' }\r\n-- The actual option is still { '*.swp' }.\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdding conversion to `nvim_get_option_value()` would still read the actual option, so it would not handle this case. We need to pass the option name and the saved value to the converter and get its structured form.",
