        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, the main thing here to distinguish are pure validation checks on the value itself, and checks against other state (i.e. other options). The naive solution would be to split validation in 2, which is probably overkill, but also irrelevant for the main here as calling `:get()` on an option shouldn't require validation which is specifically designed to throw errors without setting the option.",
